{
 "id": "M20",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "Hidden reasoning you never read is most of some bills",
 "section": "appendix",
 "order": 136,
 "caption": "The 14 most expensive runs, priced per million samples at the same rates src/analyze.py uses. Each bar splits into what you pay for: fresh input, cache writes, cache reads, the output you can read, and the reasoning you cannot.",
 "notes": [
  "Hidden reasoning reaches 87% of one run's bill. It never reaches the caller: the monitor returns a score and a sentence, and the rest is thinking you paid for and cannot read.",
  "The clearest pair is GLM-5.3. Its default and its effort=none arm cost within a couple of percent of each other, but one books 87% of that as hidden reasoning and the other 0%. The thinking did not stop, it moved into the visible channel, which is what GLM-THINKING-TOGGLE.md argues from the token counts.",
  "Data quality: this is drawn from eval logs, which are gitignored, so it reads a committed CSV derived by viz/data/derive_token_bill.py. Rerun that script when a run is added or its usage recovered, or these bars go stale without the check noticing.",
  "Only the 14 dearest of 40 priced runs are drawn, to keep the labels readable. The CSV button carries all 40, and the n=100 pilots are left out because their three runs share one recorded generation pass and so report an identical bill.",
  "Ministral 8B has no price in the table, so it has no bar. That absence is deliberate and src/analyze.py explains it."
 ],
